<title>POLAND: Poland plans 1.65 mln T 98/99 domestic sugar quota.</title>
<headline>Poland plans 1.65 mln T 98/99 domestic sugar quota.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish government's economic committee (KERM) set the sugar production quota for the domestic market at 1.65 million tonnes in the 1998/99 season, the government's press office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that KERM, which groups ministers holding economic portfolios, also decided subsidised exports in the 1999 calendar year would amount to 109,100 tonnes.</p>
<p>Poland set a 1.63 million tonne domestic quota for the 1997/98 season and allowed for 113,400 tonnes of subsidised exports.</p>
<p>The quotas have yet to be approved by the full cabinet.</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
